{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411821-what-s-your-opinion-on-exalted-vs-world-of-darkness","id":1411821,"title":"What's your opinion on Exalted vs World of Darkness?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-04T10:09:56-07:00","id":1411821,"title":"What's your opinion on Exalted vs World of Darkness?","content":"Have you played it? Read it? What do you think of it? What's your opinion of it? Any suggestions for improvements? Have you done any homebrew for it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T12:56:29-07:00","id":1411860,"title":"","content":"I've played several OWoD games and read a lot about exalted<br /> <br /> they are pretty much entirely different games, there was a point that Exalted was kinda tied in as the WoD prehistory but that fell apart pretty quickly<br /> <br /> the basic thematic difference in Exalted and WoD games is in Exalted you can quickly become a powerhouse that can challenge the very concepts that created the universe and in WoD there is a bigger fish just waiting to take notice of you and devour you in some way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T13:25:03-07:00","id":1411866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411821-what-s-your-opinion-on-exalted-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1411860#post1411860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've played several OWoD games and read a lot about exalted<br /> <br /> they are pretty much entirely different games, there was a point that Exalted was kinda tied in as the WoD prehistory but that fell apart pretty quickly<br /> <br /> the basic thematic difference in Exalted and WoD games is in Exalted you can quickly become a powerhouse that can challenge the very concepts that created the universe and in WoD there is a bigger fish just waiting to take notice of you and devour you in some way</div> </div> </div> </div>He's not referring to a fight between the Exalted gameline vs. the World of Darkness gameline; he's talking about the unofficial book in which the divine fires of old find themselves turned loose anew upon a diminished world where monsters lurk in the shadows and prey upon mortals. They're definitely not ready to rock a fight with the makers of reality in such a scenario, but there's a chance now for them to bring about a change in the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T13:28:01-07:00","id":1411867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411821-what-s-your-opinion-on-exalted-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1411860#post1411860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've played several OWoD games and read a lot about exalted<br /> <br /> they are pretty much entirely different games, there was a point that Exalted was kinda tied in as the WoD prehistory but that fell apart pretty quickly<br /> <br /> the basic thematic difference in Exalted and WoD games is in Exalted you can quickly become a powerhouse that can challenge the very concepts that created the universe and in WoD there is a bigger fish just waiting to take notice of you and devour you in some way</div> </div> </div> </div>As for the subject of the thread, I haven't played it, but I read it and found it interesting.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Edit: Removed the link at request of Admin. We don't want to get into that.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-07-2020, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T13:52:31-07:00","id":1411877,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest... my feelings about the book are heavily biased by the fact that Holden subtweeted me on Twitter for not knowing what I was talking about when I pointed out to him that he left himself open to a legitimate lawsuit from WW for how he originally posted Ex vs. WoD... but within 24 hrs later took my advice anyway. It's hard for me to enjoy the book when it's author was mean to me for helping him cover his ass.<br /> <br /> Otherwise? It's kinda Holden at his most Holden. He knows the ST system really well, and it good at brewing up stuff for it, but tends to put what he thinks is the most important thing as the most important mechanical thing, even if it's not necessarily what is actually fun about what he's making a game about. Nobody in my play circles (even those that don't know about the Twitter thing) actually wants to use it for more than ideas for other things because it's good at what it does but that's not the exact thing we want to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T19:38:14-07:00","id":1411985,"title":"","content":"The charms in Exalted v WoD are the most straightforward, readable, and narratively comprehensible they have ever been. Rating charms in value on a 1-5 scale and charging different levels of power for them, rather than creating complex trees of prerequisites, enormously simplifies both char-gen and advancement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/587-kukla","name":"Kukla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T19:49:23-07:00","id":1411989,"title":"","content":"I can\u2019t say I\u2019m much of a fan either of EX2 or WoD... Which is precisely why I love the idea of Exalted using their 2e shenanigans to dunk on WoD. I\u2019ll never actually play it but I appreciate that it exists. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T01:26:27-07:00","id":1412023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411821-what-s-your-opinion-on-exalted-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1411985#post1411985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The charms in Exalted v WoD are the most straightforward, readable, and narratively comprehensible they have ever been. Rating charms in value on a 1-5 scale and charging different levels of power for them, rather than creating complex trees of prerequisites, enormously simplifies both char-gen and advancement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh god oh god yes. You are my new friend. I love the charm system and wish normal exalted had it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T07:22:53-07:00","id":1412079,"title":"","content":"As I kind of understand it, it's written on the assumption that the Exalted are fully the Exalted in their power, and the World Of Darkness things are fully what they are. And the Exalted are limited by slow Essence mote regeneration.<br /> <br /> Then the default play mode that Holden envisoned, for Solar Exalted, which I think he described, was something like - &quot;They gather power somewhat slowly, then unleash a badass denouement on a local bunch of World of Darkness supernaturals running a local scene, then they go to ground again. Rinse and repeat.&quot;.<br /> <br /> So if that's what you want to do, it might work really well! It seems like a pretty niche story to me, but if you were a WoD + Exalted fan running scenarios in your head about Solars whaling on all the nasty WoD things for the 15 years or so that the gamelines have existed in tandem (&quot;Here comes the righteous justice of the Sun, blood drinker!&quot;), it might well be your thing.<br /> <br /> If you want something more like &quot;Marvel vs Streetfighter&quot; in which somehow assumptions of the two universes are bridged such that Ryu vs Thor somehow really is a fair fight (despite Ryu being just this guy who is a kind of street fighter, you know), then &quot;Exalted vs the WoD&quot; is really not it at all!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T09:45:59-07:00","id":1412107,"title":"","content":"I admit that I don't see the appeal of the concept, because i'm not a fan of WoD. I don't like it enough to want to mix it with Exalted, which i like, but I also don't dislike it enough to find enjoyment in making werewolves eat pavement. The 'vs WoD' part, to me, feels like it would be a speedbump to the Exalts and then you have Exalts in the modern day.<br /> <br /> And I have Shards of the Exalted Dream if I want to play Exalted Modern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T10:26:36-07:00","id":1412111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411821-what-s-your-opinion-on-exalted-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1412079#post1412079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Exalted are limited by slow Essence mote regeneration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering they get (Essence + 5) motes each day just by existing and most Charms that cost motes at all cost 1m and are scene-long (<i>including excellencies</i>)... No, they\u2019re pretty much Energizer bunnies especially by WoD standards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T13:21:07-07:00","id":1412153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411821-what-s-your-opinion-on-exalted-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1412079#post1412079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I kind of understand it, it's written on the assumption that the Exalted are fully the Exalted in their power, and the World Of Darkness things are fully what they are. And the Exalted are limited by slow Essence mote regeneration.<br /> <br /> Then the default play mode that Holden envisoned, for Solar Exalted, which I think he described, was something like - &quot;They gather power somewhat slowly, then unleash a badass denouement on a local bunch of World of Darkness supernaturals running a local scene, then they go to ground again. Rinse and repeat.&quot;.<br /> <br /> So if that's what you want to do, it might work really well! It seems like a pretty niche story to me, but if you were a WoD + Exalted fan running scenarios in your head about Solars whaling on all the nasty WoD things for the 15 years or so that the gamelines have existed in tandem (&quot;Here comes the righteous justice of the Sun, blood drinker!&quot;), it might well be your thing.<br /> <br /> If you want something more like &quot;Marvel vs Streetfighter&quot; in which somehow assumptions of the two universes are bridged such that Ryu vs Thor somehow really is a fair fight (despite Ryu being just this guy who is a kind of street fighter, you know), then &quot;Exalted vs the WoD&quot; is really not it at all!</div> </div> </div> </div>Characters in SF are, in a sense, cultivators from a lower power setting, but lower only in comparison with something like Zu Warriors, and I'm not even sure of that, because some of the higher tier characters sandbag something fierce. Gouki/Akuma, for example is explicitly that character while holding back, with Shin Akuma/Gouki being a broken, unfair SNK boss fight with a being that can do the parting of the Red Sea action with a punch (Ryu can do something similar, but it's only a pretty wide river/waterfall with a hadoken).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T02:37:35-07:00","id":1412240,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I may be underselling the raw powah of some SF characters here (particularly their &quot;stuff I can do only in cutscenes and OVA!&quot;) and also there could be other matchups in that analogic frame that would better illustrate the point. General point being that some crossovers do things to the worlds being crossed over to kind of &quot;balance&quot; them, while ExVWoD really doesn't - it's very much &quot;<i>The</i> Exalted <i>against the entire </i>World of Darkness&quot; and not &quot;Exalted <i>meets </i>World of Darkness&quot;.<br /> <br /> (The latter being a thing which Holden could've written but I guess didn't because 1) he didn't want to and 2) the sheer obscurity of rewriting the mechanics and universe to affect tweaks rather than just plonking the Exalted into the WoD - as an Exalted fan I am of course into writers deciding to write *extremely* obscure and niche stuff because its an idea that must be written, goddammit, but that definitely means a lot of uncompensated labour among writers that absolutely no one is entitled to.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T07:29:18-07:00","id":1412277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411821-what-s-your-opinion-on-exalted-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1412240#post1412240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I may be underselling the raw powah of some SF characters here (particularly their &quot;stuff I can do only in cutscenes and OVA!&quot;) and also there could be other matchups in that analogic frame that would better illustrate the point. General point being that some crossovers do things to the worlds being crossed over to kind of &quot;balance&quot; them, while ExVWoD really doesn't - it's very much &quot;<i>The</i> Exalted <i>against the entire </i>World of Darkness&quot; and not &quot;Exalted <i>meets </i>World of Darkness&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or rather, &quot;modern-day people <b>become</b> the Exalted and will probably find themselves set against <b>most of</b> the World of Darkness.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T08:43:22-07:00","id":1412296,"title":"","content":"Funny enough, I love the concept of exalted vs world of darkness. I've included world of darkness concepts and characters in my exalted games and my group loves both games. The problem is that I like Chronicles of Darkness and 3e Exalted...so when I found out the supplement in question was essentially going back towards OWoD and 2e, I decided I wouldn't be running it. I'm still happy it got put out there regardless, it's just not for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5298-novap","name":"NovaP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T13:34:40-07:00","id":1412471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411821-what-s-your-opinion-on-exalted-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1412240#post1412240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I may be underselling the raw powah of some SF characters here (particularly their &quot;stuff I can do only in cutscenes and OVA!&quot;) and also there could be other matchups in that analogic frame that would better illustrate the point. General point being that some crossovers do things to the worlds being crossed over to kind of &quot;balance&quot; them, while ExVWoD really doesn't - it's very much &quot;<i>The</i> Exalted <i>against the entire </i>World of Darkness&quot; and not &quot;Exalted <i>meets </i>World of Darkness&quot;.<br /> <br /> (The latter being a thing which Holden could've written but I guess didn't because 1) he didn't want to and 2) the sheer obscurity of rewriting the mechanics and universe to affect tweaks rather than just plonking the Exalted into the WoD - as an Exalted fan I am of course into writers deciding to write *extremely* obscure and niche stuff because its an idea that must be written, goddammit, but that definitely means a lot of uncompensated labour among writers that absolutely no one is entitled to.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;only in cutscene&quot; clause probably wouldn't hold if the characters made an appearance in a different play genre - say, a large scale brawler a la Dynasty Warriors instead of in a fighter with a mostly static 2.5D background. Then cities would know the unbridled fury of the Satsui no Hadou!<br /> <br /> Not just slam-porting the Exalted of old in is likely because of a similar issue, along with issues that crept up during the presentation of higher-Essence play - the fight would be really one-sided. During the height of 2e, Solars, Abyssals, and Infernals could double-break their Essence cap and acquire Charms that devastated an entire countryside in one attack. Sidereals have long been known to possess the broken Creation-Slaying Oblivion Kick thanks to Charcoal March of Spiders. Lunars can turn into giant, city-destroying kaijuu... though, in a hint of terrible irony, Mokole can as well, and are arguably more capable of doing so because that's a potential chargen outcome, not something that they have to wait centuries to acquire. In a one on one fight, most of these broad-scope attacks aren't more terrible than the single-hit attacks that a power made flesh could inflict, so the tight focus akin to a fighting game wouldn't necessarily change, other than for turning into a giant monster. That tends to change the fight into a whole stage or series of stages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T14:42:00-07:00","id":1412481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411821-what-s-your-opinion-on-exalted-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1412471#post1412471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sidereals have long been known to possess the broken Creation-Slaying Oblivion Kick <b>thanks to Charcoal March of Spiders</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>And to a fairly generous interpretation of what it takes for them to count as seeing people to strike them, and presumption of finding an appropriate vantage point with ease.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T15:22:03-07:00","id":1412485,"title":"","content":"Well, the Exalted have been depowered, if that's any assurance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T20:21:51-07:00","id":1412526,"title":"","content":"Thought not to below the point where Solars can yawn while they parry all six of your attacks and Lunars can walk the Spiral all the times because they feel like flipping off the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T20:42:50-07:00","id":1412527,"title":"","content":"Incoming Beans Textwall, spoilered for courtesy. EXWOD does some things I like and a lot of things I wildly do not like.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">On one hand, Holden is trying to patch up some of the more abrasive parts of the OWOD rules in EXWOD; Exalts' areas of expertise ignore the &quot;1s subtract successes&quot; rule, the Ability list is meant to be unified rather than variable, and combat uses the DAV20 initiative system instead of the more finnicky standard one. Also, boiling down Charms has some nice effects, and in some ways it's got shades of an easier Exalted system. The translation of Caste/Aspect Abilities goes nicely in some places, like giving Firearms to Air and Journeys, or Finance to Wood.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, do you like OWOD? Do you like the OWOD engine, and the OWOD combat system? You'd better, because you're still stuck with it, Holden's bandaids aside. Meanwhile, while EX3 is in some ways shaving down some of the power-gaps, EXWOD exacerbates them. For instance, a standard starting Solar at Essence Rating 1 has a total mote pool of 10. A starting Dragon-Blood at Essence Rating 1 has a total mote pool of 5. The highest a Dragon-Blood's mote pool can ever go is 10. This is irksome to me, as are about a thousand other little things, like kind of clumsy writing that makes it hard for me to understand very important details of things. Then there's also the fact that, given the lack of a social system in OWOD, most social charms are either &quot;your roll is gooder&quot; or &quot;MIND CONTROL LASER&quot;. Then there's Infernals, where he seemingly tries to balance out overtuned charms with undertuned Excellency coverage and just makes two wrongs instead of a right. Annnnnd there's the way Alchemicals share the lowest starting Attribute dots with Dragon-Bloods (which itself is a thing we left behind in 3e), which is pretty unpleasant given they're Attribute-based Exalts. Also, remember those Caste/Aspect Ability spreads? Well, sometimes they mismatch badly with Charms. Eclipses and Moonshadows get some vehicular charms, including one to summon a magic car/motorcycle/whatever, but they don't get Drive while Dawns and Dusks do, which strikes me as a bit odd.<br /> <br /> My TL;DR for this is essentially... EXWOD deserves credit for making me and probably like five other people want to convert it to something else, and having some legitimately good concepts in it. It then, in my opinion, burns that credit as the initial &quot;oh, that's neat&quot; gives way to the disappointment of finding the whole thing is covered with a host of jammy hamster pawprints. If you love OWOD, you're probably fine. If the OWOD engine irks you, grab the PDFs to loot for ideas for some other thing, they're free.<br /> <br /> Oh, and as much as the referential header fonts are clever, I also dislike them.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T04:20:10-07:00","id":1412566,"title":"","content":"As I run a game of Exalted in the early Bronze Age of the World of Darkness, I vaguely thought about giving it a proper look at some point, but this thread has convinced me that it's probably not worth it. Might as well stick with the Ex3 rules that we know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T06:01:24-07:00","id":1412585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411821-what-s-your-opinion-on-exalted-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1412566#post1412566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I run a game of Exalted in the early Bronze Age of the World of Darkness, I vaguely thought about giving it a proper look at some point, but this thread has convinced me that it's probably not worth it. Might as well stick with the Ex3 rules that we know.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the PDFs are free. If nothing else, it\u2019s worth reading to mine for ideas. And it\u2019s not bad. It\u2019s old-school Storyteller with some definite 2e-isms, and could have really used a beta, but I enjoyed reading them, particularly the storytelling/why I did it that way/night people chapters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T06:02:43-07:00","id":1412586,"title":"","content":"*looks around*<br /> <br /> *likes ExvWoD*<br /> <br /> *slinks off sadly*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T07:02:59-07:00","id":1412592,"title":"","content":"I don't much care for it. It's a nice meme at most, and an exercise in imagining how big the schadenfreude would get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T08:10:10-07:00","id":1412601,"title":"","content":"I'm generally positive on ExVsWoD. I think it's a really fun read, well thought out and put together, and about as mechanically good as could be hoped building on WoD20. Not super likely ill ever run it, but some lunatic converted it to MET and it would be really fun to throw an Exalt past players in a WoD LARP just to confuse the hell out of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T11:50:59-07:00","id":1412625,"title":"","content":"I cannot really imagine anybody doing a better job.<br /> <br /> Like, I literally cannot imagine anybody setting out to do this particular thing, and coming up with a better final work that doesn't either a) fail to resemble the Exalted, b) fail to resemble the World of Darkness, or c) just kind of fail to work at all.<br /> <br /> You can complain about the specific compromises Holden had to make but I can't imagine anybody else doing one with <i>no </i>compromises, even if they had a budget.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T13:44:26-07:00","id":1412638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411821-what-s-your-opinion-on-exalted-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1412485#post1412485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Exalted have been depowered, if that's any assurance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually that kind of touches on why I don't find the concept to be that interesting. Like, if you have to take a tire iron to the kneecaps of one side in a crossover to retain some measure of balance between the two sides <i>it might not be a good idea to cross them over</i>.<br /> <br /> Like, that's kind of admitting &quot;Hey if we take the power tiers as they are supposed to be, this will be a cakewalk for the Exalts, so they had to be depowered somehow to make it fair&quot; which in turn goes back to the whole &quot;I don't find this an interesting crossover premise because the outcome seems assured&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T15:00:58-07:00","id":1412644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411821-what-s-your-opinion-on-exalted-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1412638#post1412638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually that kind of touches on why I don't find the concept to be that interesting. Like, if you have to take a tire iron to the kneecaps of one side in a crossover to retain some measure of balance between the two sides <i>it might not be a good idea to cross them over</i>.<br /> <br /> Like, that's kind of admitting &quot;Hey if we take the power tiers as they are supposed to be, this will be a cakewalk for the Exalts, so they had to be depowered somehow to make it fair&quot; which in turn goes back to the whole &quot;I don't find this an interesting crossover premise because the outcome seems assured&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I, uh, don't think they've been depowered all <i>that</i> much. A Dawn Caste with Fivefold Bulwark Stance and an Excellency is damn near untouchable physically, and you could afford Integrity-Protecting Prana to shut out mind control as well. That's without spending any freebie points.<br /> <br /> I'm sure a mage could find some way to trouble the Solar, but he could probably thrash a coterie of vampires or pack of Garou without blinking.<br /> <br /> They would certainly have needed depowering to make it fair. It isn't fair at all. It'd probably get more interesting if you pitted Solars against Methuselahs (which the books do suggest) or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T19:02:45-07:00","id":1412661,"title":"","content":"I've played it. It's very nice, but I'd like some more stuff to it--I'd really like full Alchemicals, and I think they need to be empowered a bit. (but I'm an alchemical fanboy). <br /> <br /> It's important to note that while you <i>can</i> exalt as a Kinfolk or Ghoul, the default assumption for the setting is that you exalt with <i>no idea</i> of what is going on. This is a big deal, because it's going to inform a huge part of your game. The assumption for most settings is that say, <br /> Catch Vamp snacking on boyfriend.<br /> INSTANT SOLAR POWER!<br /> Totally murderize vamp, his friends and likely anyone else that looks vampirish...<br /> Realize that you have no idea what is going on, and every vamp in the city is now hunting you. <br /> <br /> Which is fun, But...<br /> <br /> Okay, one thing I really would have liked would have been at least a few suggestions for... Six months later, a year later, etc. What happens when you start learning about the WOD? When the Abyssal has had time to sit down with some ghosts and chat about the mages and vampires and werewolves, oh my?<br /> <br /> I mean, I can see why not, given that part of the fun of Exalted is that there isn't so much a metaplot as &quot;what am I pointing my howitzer at today!&quot; But it would have been interesting, especially suggestions for higher power exalts.<br /> <br /> For myself, I'm getting ready to put together a one year later campaign set on the &quot;Free City of Detroit&quot; where no less than twenty of the Chosen have established their domain. It looks to be interesting...<br /> <br /> One thing I will say, is that I like it, because it's not as <i>complex</i> as 3E and I'm seriously considering, at least until Exalted Essence comes out, just using it for any Exalted games period.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T20:07:14-07:00","id":1412667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411821-what-s-your-opinion-on-exalted-vs-world-of-darkness#post1411821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you played it? Read it? What do you think of it? What's your opinion of it? Any suggestions for improvements? Have you done any homebrew for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I read it. I liked it, but I probably wouldn\u2019t use it personally. My personal headcanon (borrowed from someone who basically taught me Exalted and whose opinion I respect) is that Exalted is not the distant past of the WoD, it\u2019s a pocket dimension in the Middle Umbral Realm called the Flux Realm, an island of stability in a vast Wyld zone. That being said, I liked the mechanics presented in Ex vs WoD and I really liked the setting it portrayed. I\u2019m just not a big fan of epic Clash of Worlds type games, so I\u2019m not sure how useful it would be for my campaign if I ran one. But I was defo impressed.<br /> <br /> Hope this helps \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T10:56:51-07:00","id":1416302,"title":"","content":"I can't believe this slipped past me for as long as it did; mostly finished reading the main book, have peeked a bit at the follow-up Companion book. As someone who was a huge fan of classic WoD and got into Exalted from its connections to it, this is the sort of thing that would have made me squirm in ecstacy a decade ago! These days, I'm more of the opinion that the more distance between the two gamelines, the better, and I openly wish that the few vestiges of WoD in Exalted be removed. But I still had a TON of fun with this! <br /> <br /> The Charms were a particular high point, as has been mentioned. Part of the draw of Vampire to me has always been the straight-forward simplicity...I can introduce that game to people who don't know what roleplaying is, and have them rolling in a half-hour! That sort of quick and easy simplicity was always an appeal of White Wolf and tbh, I feel like that's getting lost. As though some working for WW are kinda embarrassed by it, and run on the idea that &quot;real&quot; gamers like heavy crunch...Storypath seems geared towards that in a way; it's actually not that complex, but it strives to give the *illusion* of complexity. But, yeah, the mild headache of having to learn *yet another* alternate version of the charm sets was offset by how cool and easy it all was TO learn. I'll be surprised if not a few players go, &quot;Can we...just use this for ALL our games now?&quot;<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Really appreciated the humor, too! One of my favorite bits was Holden warning against have mixed PCs including various Exalts and obscure Supernaturals for thematic reasons...only to immediately reverse that, and *encourage* such a campaign, where they all ride around in a car beating up antediluvians...and then suggests detailing this game session to the folks at the White Wolf booth at a gaming convention, just so you can watch the light slowly die in their eyes in real time!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> While on the subject of WoD: afaic, it ended with Time of Judgement. I completely bought into their stated reasons for ending it, and embraced the New WoD, which in many ways, I actually like better! I was frankly shocked when they brought OWoD back, and rebranded NWoD, as if to tacitly admit that it wasn't that good or selling that great, and now we're in some sort of Marvel/Ultimate Marvel situation. I wonder if this is sustainable, or if it's just a matter of time until they cancel CoD, or merge it with WoD (if only by introducing things unique to it like Prometheans and Deviants).<br /> <br /> I'll be honest, I haven't looked at any of the new, revived stuff. I'm sure it's good, but how similar is it to the OWoD stuff? Times and culture have changed, so I guess it's not as In Your Face as it was in the 90s? Is it still Metaplot heavy? Does it reference the ToJ at all, or is this like an alternate setting where none of that happened? Are there any plans to introduce the newer games, like Promethean and Beast?<br /> <br /> If I could ask Holden any one thing, it would be on the feasibility of adapting this book to CoD, and whether he'd be up to the task...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T22:13:08-07:00","id":1416415,"title":"","content":"It's also interesting to compare ExVsWoD to the Modern Shards directly, esp. Burn Legend. The fact that BL doesn't really flesh out its background so that it's also set in (something like) our real world, and shares a similar set up with the Dragon-Blooded esp makes a homebrewed combo workable. Since the one lacks Martial Arts and the other lacks Charms, maybe they can cover each others' lack, by porting Martial Arts Techniques and Overdrive into ExVsWoD and Charms into BL? Hmm...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T22:20:33-07:00","id":1416419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411821-what-s-your-opinion-on-exalted-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1416415#post1416415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also interesting to compare ExVsWoD to the Modern Shards directly, esp. Burn Legend. The fact that BL doesn't really flesh out its background so that it's also set in (something like) our real world, and shares a similar set up with the Dragon-Blooded esp makes a homebrewed combo workable. Since the one lacks Martial Arts and the other lacks Charms, maybe they can cover each others' lack, by porting Martial Arts Techniques and Overdrive into ExVsWoD and Charms into BL? Hmm...</div> </div> </div> </div>*raises eyebrows*<br /> <br /> You sure that ExvWoD doesn't have martial arts charms? I see several references to it in-text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T22:32:55-07:00","id":1416423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411821-what-s-your-opinion-on-exalted-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1416419#post1416419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*raises eyebrows*<br /> <br /> You sure that ExvWoD doesn't have martial arts charms? I see several references to it in-text.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Holden goes on at length about why he left them out and the in-universe explanation for their lack in the Companion...but for those who still want them, he substitutes the Qiao of the Shih for them (Devil Fighter Style, for ex). Aside from that, Exalted fighters use RL styles backed up with Essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T22:37:54-07:00","id":1416427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411821-what-s-your-opinion-on-exalted-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1416423#post1416423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, Holden goes on at length about why he left them out and the in-universe explanation for their lack in the Companion...but for those who still want them, he substitutes the Qiao of the Shih for them (Devil Fighter Style, for ex). Aside from that, Exalted fighters use RL styles backed up with Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be frank I'm no fan of the martial arts charms. For starters, you have to constantly balance them against literally every single other charm in the book. And secondly, I've seen some people do good charms. You roll to get some effects, and pay willpower for the others. So mortals don't need essence pools to pull off any bullshit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T03:52:45-07:00","id":1416459,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve played it. In fact, though things are about a month and a half into a break, the game is still ongoing. <br /> ExWoD is fun! At its base, it\u2019s just plain fun. We\u2019ve had a Sidereal (Journeys), a Solar (Zenith), an Abyssal (Day), and an Infernal (no castes). We\u2019ve just added a Lunar and a 7th Gen Kiasyd, but I haven\u2019t seen them in action yet.<br /> <br /> The game has lots of clunky bits\u2014Infernals are particularly unbalanced, getting the best of a couple things by a large margin, and getting straight screwed on some others, but pretty much every part works like it\u2019s supposed to work. Solars are a holy terror for Vampires, Abyssals are the S-class of killing things, etc. <br /> <br /> Seriously, the only part that really seems to be an issue is the fact that it was designed for the OWoD, and not the newer Chronicles. And if you\u2019re a dyed-in-the-wool WoD partisan, like me, that\u2019s not really an issue at all.<br /> <br /> Bottom line: If you\u2019ve ever wanted to just wreck the careful balance between Vampire factions, or stomp on some Wan-Kuei, play this game!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1536-39steps","name":"39Steps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T03:58:36-07:00","id":1416460,"title":"","content":"*cheers as thread is revived with actual play*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T06:37:13-07:00","id":1416471,"title":"","content":"&quot;Have you played it? &quot;<br /> <br /> Nope<br /> <br /> Read it?<br /> <br /> Yup<br /> <br /> &quot;What do you think of it? What's your opinion of it?&quot;<br /> <br /> I liked it, but it kinda leaves out my favorite part of Exalted, which is that in Exalted the abilities and powers of the Chosen grow in all dimensions of possible power. For example, a Dawn and a Twighlight and an Eclipse all have radically different but radically potent abilities to change the world. Someone can be a super-diplomat and that translates into meaningful powers and meaningful reactions within the fiction. One of Exalted's core strengths, to me, is that it makes (or at least tries to make) those aspects of plays as meaningful, important and accessible as the climactic battle scene.<br /> <br /> Exalted vs WoD is all about the climactic battle scene. That's what the author was writing the book for. That's the story he was interested in allowing play for. I'm just not as interested in that story. I can get that from other systems without worrying about the baggage of the OWoD system that I dislike anyway.<br /> <br /> &quot; Any suggestions for improvements?&quot;<br /> <br /> There are certainly things I would do differently, and things I dislike about the game; but these ae things that would fundamentally change what the game is about. It's like.. although I like Exalted and I like WoD and I like the idea of a mash-up, I don't really want a mash up that tries to be the game played in this way. If I wanted a game that played the way ExVsWoD plays, the version that's out there is perfect for it. If I tried to &quot;improve&quot; it, I wouldn't be improving it so much as changing it from the game it's trying to play to the game I'd rather be playing. So, it wouldn't be honest or appropriate of me to claim I could improve on it.<br /> <br /> &quot;Have you done any homebrew for it?&quot;<br /> <br /> Nah, though it has inspired me to do a lot more work on a homebrew game sort of like Exalted Vs WoD. And then I abandoned that possible game; as one does when one is a TTRP gamer =D","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":2711,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","user":"Janissary87","date":". 10-02-2020, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T13:25:55-07:00","id":1416523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411821-what-s-your-opinion-on-exalted-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1412661#post1412661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For myself, I'm getting ready to put together a one year later campaign set on the &quot;Free City of Detroit&quot; where no less than twenty of the Chosen have established their domain. It looks to be interesting...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>ooh interesting?<br /> <br /> Not agree with it all but part campaign module, and insightful design document with help testing for the long awaited idea and insights on methods chosen. Fitting into the oWoD system<br /> yep favors Solars in power but DBs, as always, get the everything else<br /> <br /> not played, only read.<br /> particularly happy just for giving SOME consideration to the imbued even with the suggestion of don't. But gives enough insight I feel can try to mod to 'go your own waaaay'<br /> Sections/essays like Reconciling Cross-Game Systems, Magical Items, Design subtitle General Considerations in Last chapter, Whither the Great Curse? from the same, Hedge Magic Errata from the supplement,<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forums.spacebattles.com/threads/exalted-vs-the-world-of-darkness.737872/post-70504313\" target=\"_blank\">Trying to blend them, some,</a> with Imbued as prototype 'Heroic' Exalted. their schtick being lowered difficulty to exploding dice and limitless recovery and development... always at a mortal-ish base.<br /> <br /> I might want to add a medical system but that's a general preference. But I feel bypasses 'the novel' preference of WW/OPP and more the game instructions while still having character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1498-darmani","name":"Darmani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1498_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T14:09:46-07:00","id":1416530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411821-what-s-your-opinion-on-exalted-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1416302#post1416302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't believe this slipped past me for as long as it did; mostly finished reading the main book, have peeked a bit at the follow-up Companion book. As someone who was a huge fan of classic WoD and got into Exalted from its connections to it, this is the sort of thing that would have made me squirm in ecstacy a decade ago! These days, I'm more of the opinion that the more distance between the two gamelines, the better, and I openly wish that the few vestiges of WoD in Exalted be removed. But I still had a TON of fun with this! <br /> <br /> The Charms were a particular high point, as has been mentioned. Part of the draw of Vampire to me has always been the straight-forward simplicity...I can introduce that game to people who don't know what roleplaying is, and have them rolling in a half-hour! That sort of quick and easy simplicity was always an appeal of White Wolf and tbh, I feel like that's getting lost. As though some working for WW are kinda embarrassed by it, and run on the idea that &quot;real&quot; gamers like heavy crunch...Storypath seems geared towards that in a way; it's actually not that complex, but it strives to give the *illusion* of complexity. But, yeah, the mild headache of having to learn *yet another* alternate version of the charm sets was offset by how cool and easy it all was TO learn. I'll be surprised if not a few players go, &quot;Can we...just use this for ALL our games now?&quot;<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Really appreciated the humor, too! One of my favorite bits was Holden warning against have mixed PCs including various Exalts and obscure Supernaturals for thematic reasons...only to immediately reverse that, and *encourage* such a campaign, where they all ride around in a car beating up antediluvians...and then suggests detailing this game session to the folks at the White Wolf booth at a gaming convention, just so you can watch the light slowly die in their eyes in real time!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> While on the subject of WoD: afaic, it ended with Time of Judgement. I completely bought into their stated reasons for ending it, and embraced the New WoD, which in many ways, I actually like better! I was frankly shocked when they brought OWoD back, and rebranded NWoD, as if to tacitly admit that it wasn't that good or selling that great, and now we're in some sort of Marvel/Ultimate Marvel situation. I wonder if this is sustainable, or if it's just a matter of time until they cancel CoD, or merge it with WoD (if only by introducing things unique to it like Prometheans and Deviants).<br /> <br /> I'll be honest, I haven't looked at any of the new, revived stuff. I'm sure it's good, but how similar is it to the OWoD stuff? Times and culture have changed, so I guess it's not as In Your Face as it was in the 90s? Is it still Metaplot heavy? Does it reference the ToJ at all, or is this like an alternate setting where none of that happened? Are there any plans to introduce the newer games, like Promethean and Beast?<br /> <br /> If I could ask Holden any one thing, it would be on the feasibility of adapting this book to CoD, and whether he'd be up to the task...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You are the first person I\u2019ve met on here who agrees with me that maybe merging WoD and CoD by introducing things like Prometheans, Beasts and Deviants to WoD wouldn\u2019t be such a terrible idea. I\u2019ve largely given up on the idea, but...<br /> <br /> Ofc if they did it would probably just lead to a big chronicle arc to unmerge them years later, so maybe not lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 10-02-2020, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}